/**
 * Custom footer that replaces pi's built-in footer.
 *
 * The header shows the model, thinking level, and session. A separate line below
 * it shows each skill in the effective context and its token age. Wide terminals
 * get a labeled footer: a
 * location line, a context line (graded gauge + current/window tokens + cumulative
 * cost + average $/turn), and a cache line (session hit rate, latest cache result,
 * and reused/new tokens). Narrow terminals (≤56 cols) collapse to two compact lines.
 *
 * Skill age starts at the first valid assistant prompt after each load and uses
 * provider-reported input+cacheRead+cacheWrite. Context fill counts input+output+cacheRead+
 * cacheWrite of the last valid assistant turn (see calculateContextTokens,
 * dist/core/compaction/compaction.js), surfaced via ctx.getContextUsage(). Cache
 * hit is cacheRead / (input+cacheRead+cacheWrite). A significant latest-turn miss
 * compares cacheRead with the prior prompt, matching pi's 1,024-token noise floor.
 *
 * Reacts to session_start, session_shutdown, session_compact, session_tree,
 * model_select, thinking_level_select, message_end, turn_end, and the inter-extension
 * "session:name-changed" event (coupled to emitter `../auto-session-name/index.ts`)
